# The annotations of the game image $6D42-$FFFF (the YS 63 covertape's CODE block, TZX block 13): the single source
# of truth for src/game/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py --case .). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# Witness: "L1 N (builds)" is the number of entries into a routine summed over the builds of case.json
# (read_builds and code_builds: c1, menu, hiscore, lives, timer and the 32 RZX cave windows rzx01-rzx32), from
# work/stage2/entry-runs.txt (work/stage2/execs.py). Cave 4 is counted from stage 2's rzx04, replayed to the cave's
# end (work/stage2/rzx04/cap, the build case.json names); the stage-1 rzx04, whose replay lost the RZX at frame 2344,
# is not counted (its counts were swapped for cap's in review round 1). Stage 2's death-crush and death-fire
# (tests/inputs, tools/move_script.py) are not in the sums (case.json witness_skip); their witnesses are named where used.
# kit/mkgame.py checks every such line against the builds and prints a stale one (--fix-witness rewrites it).
# "Known only from the code" marks what no build ran or read.
# Coordinates: the cave is 30 x 20 cells, CaveGrid $FDA8 + 30 x row + column (row 0 at the top); a cell is drawn
# 2 x 2 characters, the window is 16 x 11 cells on character rows 0-21.

@equ $028E RomKeyScan ; the ROM's KEY-SCAN: E = the key, $FF when none
@equ $03B5 RomBeeper ; the ROM's BEEPER: HL = the period, DE = the cycles
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the display file
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen attributes

@isub $7F04 LD HL,HiScoreTable-9
@isub $7F60 LD HL,HiScoreTable-15
@isub $7F90 LD HL,HiScoreTable-15
@isub $7FDE LD HL,HiScoreTable-9
@isub $82BA LD HL,CaveData-314
@isub $8356 LD HL,Font-256
@isub $8784 LD DE,CaveGrid-1
@isub $8B17 LD DE,ScrollerText+434
@isub $8913 LD H,NotePeriods/256
@isub $8927 LD H,NotePeriods/256
@isub $8982 ADD A,(LogoPixels-Screen)/256
@isub $87B3 LD DE,CaveGrid-2
@isub $92DF LD HL,CaveNames-20
@isub $95A5 LD DE,CaveGrid-1
@isub $9980 LD DE,CaveGrid-1
@isub $E8B2 LD HL,$F1F2
@isub $E8B5 LD DE,$F1F2
@isub $EE3B ADD A,CaveTunes&255
@isub $EE3E LD D,CaveTunes/256

@module hiscore ; The high-score table, the name entry, the game-over screen and the scroller
@about HiScoreTable $FD14 holds 5 records of 15 bytes: 6 score digits (0-9 a byte, not ASCII) and a 9-character name. After a game GameOver $7FF3 compares ScoreDigits $FD94 with each record from the top (HiScoreCompare $7F60); the first record the score is not below takes it (HiScoreInsert $7F7A): the lower records move down one, the fifth is lost, and the name is typed in (EnterName $7F00). Then the game-over screen (GameOverScreen $8BD5).
@about When the title tune runs out, the menu shows the table (ShowHiScores $B2E4) and runs the scroller ScrollerText $6D42 along the bottom line until a key of half row 1-5 is pressed or the text ends.

$6D42 t ScrollerText ; The menu scroller's text: 433 ASCII characters and a 0 end mark
> RunScroller $8AEB prints one character a step at the right end of the bottom line and scrolls the line left 8 pixels (ScrollBottomLine $8AAC) between characters. The text names the 1990 features (anti-gravity, 4D teleport, forcefields, bubbles, elixirs, "jumping jelly beans"), the keys G (abort), H (quit screen) and F (map), and "(C) 1990 MICHAEL BATTY".
> Witness: the menu recording reads the whole text: 3472 ScrollBottomLine calls = 434 x 8, frames 3284-5478, the last character the 0 end mark.
@res texts/scroller.bin

@module music ; The tune player and the tunes
@about PlayTune $88CE plays a tune of 4-byte notes with interrupts off: [drum, n1, n2, length]. Drum 1 calls ROM BEEPER with HL = $020B, DE = 3 before the note, drum 2 with HL = $0106, DE = 5 (two clicks of different pitch); other values nothing. n1 and n2 index NotePeriods $BC00 (a big-endian word at $BC00 + 2n): two counters toggle bit 4 of port $FE, each at its own period, for length x 256 loop turns. The tune ends at the record whose n1 is $FF, or when a key of half row 1-5 (port $F7FE) is down. HL returns pointing at the n1 byte of the record where it stopped (past its drum byte): the menu compares HL with $B269, the $FF byte of TitleTune's end record, to know the tune ran out.
@about The tunes: the title TitleTune $AD00, the game over GameOverTune $AA00, the extra life LifeTune $AC5F, the win WinTune $6EF4, the map MapTune $E8E8 and eight cave tunes, one per four caves (CaveTunes $EE24; the 1988 version played CaveTune1 $BB80 in every cave).

$6EF4 b WinTune 4 ; The tune after cave 32: 258 notes, the last record $FF,$FF at $72FC
> Played by WinGame $A8BF through PlayWinTune $A615. Witness: the rzx32 build reads $6EF4-$6F5F (its first 27 notes) before the recording ends; the rest is known only from the code.
@res music/win.bin
$72FE b WinTunePad ; Leftover: two $FF bytes after the win tune
> No code reads them (known only from the code).
@res leftovers/win-pad.bin

@module effects ; The beeper effects, the noise loops and the teleport's attribute flash
@about Every sound but the tunes goes through ROM BEEPER $03B5 (HL = the period, DE = the cycles) or a loop that sends bit 4 of port $FE. One sound a pass is chosen by PassSound $E83A: a thud (ThudSound $8228) when a boulder landed or was pushed, else the fall noise (FallSound $E7A9) when an object fell. The gem, the exit, the timer, the death and the specials make their own sounds when they happen.

$7300 b TeleportFrames 32 ; Four attribute screens of 768 bytes the teleport effect copies to $5800 in turn
> TeleportFlashOut $9230 and TeleportFlashIn $924F step AnimPhase $FD72 up or down (0-3) and copy frame AnimPhase ($7300 + 768 x phase) to the attributes. Witness: the rzx builds read all four frames.
@res graphics/teleport-frames.bin

@module hiscore
$7F00 c EnterName ; Type a name into a high-score record
> HL = the record's name field (9 bytes), B = the record (1-5; the screen row is 2B + 10). Each key comes from WaitKey $8C1D (KeyTable $A900 gives its character) and is printed and stored; '0' deletes the last character, 'e' (ENTER) ends. Writes the name in place.
> Witness: L1 1 (hiscore).
$7F0A EnterNameLoop
$7F12 EnterNameLoop2
$7F26 EnterNameSkip
$7F3A EnterNameSkip2
$7F49 EnterNameSkip3
$7F60 c HiScoreCompare ; Compare the score with high-score record B
> B = the record (1-5). HL = HiScoreTable + 15 x (B - 1), DE = ScoreDigits $FD94; the 6 digits are compared from the first. Out: carry set when the score is below the record, else carry clear.
> Witness: L1 9 (hiscore, lives).
$7F66 HiScoreCompareLoop
$7F6E HiScoreCompareLoop2
$7F74 HiScoreCompareSkip
$7F7A c HiScoreInsert ; Put the score into the table if it is not below a record
> Tries records 1-5 with HiScoreCompare $7F60. At the first the score is not below: ClearScreen, the lower records move down one (the fifth is lost), the score digits and a blank name go in, EnterName $7F00. Returns with no change when every record is above the score.
> Witness: L1 2 (hiscore, lives).
$7F7C HiScoreInsertLoop
$7F8A HiScoreInsertSkip
$7F96 HiScoreInsertLoop2
$7FAA HiScoreInsertLoop3
$7FBF HiScoreInsertSkip2
$7FE4 HiScoreInsertLoop4
$7FE9 HiScoreInsertLoop5
$7FF3 c GameOver ; The end of a game: the high-score check, then the game-over screen
> HiScoreInsert $7F7A, GameOverScreen $8BD5. Called from NewGame $8BE5 after the last life.
> Witness: L1 2 (hiscore, lives).

@module cells ; The cell update: gravity, rolling, crushing, the switch, the animation codes
@about Once a pass ScanCells $8075 walks CaveGrid from row 18, column 29 back to row 0, column 0 (each row right to left, the rows upward), DE the cell below. Earth 6, empty 0, wall 5, force field 9, bubble $0E, teleporter $0D, the exit 1, the switch box $0B, the player 3 / 4 and the codes above $10 ($11-$1F) are skipped ($10 itself reaches MoveObject $80DB); boulders 2, gems 7, jelly beans 8, anti-gravity arrows $0A, potions $0C and fire $0F fall (MoveObject $80DB). Row 19 is never a source: nothing falls out of the cave.
@about An object falls one cell when the cell below is empty; the cell it left gets $20 (just vacated: nothing falls or rolls into it this pass; ClearVacated $81AC clears the marks at the next pass). If the cell under the object's new place is the player, the player is killed (Crush $9ABC); if it is a switch box, SwitchHit $7FFC is set. When the cell below is not empty the object rolls off anything but the player, earth or a vacated cell: to the left when the left cell and the one below it are empty, else to the right the same way; the object goes to the side cell, its old cell and the cell under the side cell get $20. A boulder above fire becomes the dissolve animation $15 instead.
@about In the caves whose earth graphic is the $A4xx one (13, 17, 22, 24, 26) earth falls too: SetEarthFalls $FB81 patches the earth test of the scan away. Falling earth never crushes the player (EarthFallGuard $9AA6). With anti-gravity on (AntiGravSteps $FD8D not 0) AntiGravPass $A7CD runs the upward scan AntiGravScan $A655 instead: objects rise.

$7FFA b FlagsPad ; Leftover: a byte before the flags, never read
$7FFB b FizzCount ; The fizz countdown: 7 when a boulder stands over fire (the scan's dissolve); FizzSound $A773 beeps while it runs down
$7FFC b SwitchHit ; $FF when a falling object landed on a switch box; SwitchClear $817A then clears the force fields
$7FFD b PlayerKilled ; $FF when the player is killed: crushed by a falling object or walked into fire
$7FFE b ObjectFell ; $FF when an object other than a boulder fell this pass (the fall noise)
$7FFF b BoulderFell ; $FF when a boulder fell this pass (the fall noise)

@module renderer ; The cell table, the cell graphics and the cave window
@about The screen shows a window of 16 x 11 cells of the 30 x 20 cave; a cell is 16 x 16 pixels (2 x 2 characters) with its own 4 attributes. CellGraphicsTable $8000 gives the graphic of each cell code 0-31 (the low 5 bits of the cell). A graphic is 36 bytes: 4 attributes (top left, top right, bottom right, bottom left), then 32 pixel bytes in zigzag order (even pixel lines left then right, odd lines right then left), drawn by DrawCell $8F60.
@about The animated cells are animated by rewriting their table words each pass (AnimateCells $900B: the player; AnimateTable $90B2: the specials and, in the falling-earth caves, the earth and empty frames) and the gem colour bytes (DrawPass $8D46). The cave's earth and wall words are set from its parameters (CaveSetup $9313).

$8000 w CellGraphicsTable 1 ; The graphic of each cell code 0-31: 32 addresses of 36-byte graphics
> Read through CellGraphicAddr $8D66 by DrawCell $8F60 (every cell drawn, in every build). Words 3 and 4 (the player), 6 and 5 (earth, wall) and the animated words 8, 9, 10 and 12-15 are rewritten during play, and word 0 (the empty cell) in the falling-earth caves: EarthAnimStep $FB70 points it at a frame of EmptyFrames $FAE0 each pass, and SetEarthFalls $FB84 puts BlankGraphic $AA72 back at every cave start. Words 16 and 21 ($8020, $802A) are never read: the codes $10 and $15 step on (AnimateCellCodes $937E) before the window is drawn in the same pass. Words 1 (the exit: it flashes by its attributes, ExitFlash $905B), 2 (the boulder), 7 (the gem: DrawPass $8D46 cycles its attribute bytes) and 11 (the switch) are never written (code and the state logs). Words 28-31 are $0000: no such cells.
$8002 CellExitGfx ; cell 1
$8004 CellBoulderGfx ; cell 2
$8006 CellPlayerRightGfx ; cell 3
$8008 CellPlayerLeftGfx ; cell 4
$800A CellWallGfx ; cell 5
$800C CellEarthGfx ; cell 6
$800E CellGemGfx ; cell 7
$8010 CellJellyBeanGfx ; cell 8
$8012 CellForceFieldGfx ; cell 9
$8014 CellAntiGravGfx ; cell 10
$8016 CellSwitchGfx ; cell 11
$8018 CellPotionGfx ; cell 12
$801A CellTeleporterGfx ; cell 13
$801C CellBubbleGfx ; cell 14
$801E CellFireGfx ; cell 15
$8020 CellBurstGfx ; cell 16 ($10-$14: the bubble burst frames)
$802A CellDissolveGfx ; cell 21 ($15-$1B: the boulder dissolving in fire)
$8038 CellUnusedGfx ; cell 28 (28-31: no such cells, $0000)

$8040 c PrintGlyph ; Print an 8 x 8 glyph at a character cell
> B = the character row (0-23), C = the column (0-31), DE = the 8 glyph bytes. Out: DE past the glyph, HL the last screen byte. The font, the HUD digits and the map glyphs go through it.
> Witness: L1 90104 (c1, hiscore, lives, menu, timer, rzx x32).
$8051 PrintGlyphLoop

@module mapscreen ; The map screen (key F): the whole cave as 8 x 8 glyphs
@about Key F (half row $FD, bit 3) shows the whole 30 x 20 cave once per cave (MapShown $EA8D): ShowMap $EA80 draws a frame of MapFrameGlyphs $E9C0, every cell as an 8 x 8 glyph of MapGlyphs $9A00 (DrawMapCells $8059) coloured from MapAttrs $9A80 (ColourMapCells $81CC), plays MapTune $E8E8 and redraws the cave window.

$8059 c DrawMapCells ; Draw the 600 cells as 8 x 8 glyphs, from the last cell back
> HL = the grid's last cell $FFFF, B = 20 rows, C = 30 columns, D = $9A (LD D,$9A at $8060); a cell of code k is the glyph MapGlyphs + 8k, printed by MapCellGlyph $E9AE at row B, column C.
> Witness: L1 1 (timer).
$805E b DrawMapCellsOverlap ; LD C,$1E and the first byte of LD D,$9A: bytes that are two instruction streams
> From $8059 the code runs LD C,$1E ($805E) and LD D,$9A ($8060). The column loop's JR NZ,$805F enters at $805F, which runs LD E,$16 and SBC A,$D ($8061): both results are overwritten at once (LD A,(HL), LD E,A), so the side entry is harmless. mkgame keeps the overlapped bytes as data (the code at $8061 is the side entry's).
$8061 c DrawMapCellsLoop ; The per-cell body of DrawMapCells (entered at SBC A,D)
> E = 8 x the cell, MapCellGlyph $E9AE; HL, C and B step down; the row loop DJNZ goes back to $805E.
> Witness: L1 580 (timer).

@module cells
$8075 c ScanCells ; The gravity scan of a pass: clear the fall flags, then ScanCellsBody
> A = 0, JP ClearFallFlags $E7F5, which clears BoulderLanded $E7A8 and BoulderFell $7FFF and jumps to ScanCellsBody $8079.
> Witness: L1 42379 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8079 c ScanCellsBody ; Walk the grid bottom-up, right to left, and move each falling object
> ObjectFell $7FFE = A (0). HL = $FFE1 (row 18, column 29), DE = HL + 30, 19 rows of 30 cells. A boulder above fire becomes $15 (the dissolve) and FizzCount $7FFB = 7. The cells skipped (see the module header) never reach EarthFallGuard $9AA6 / MoveObject $80DB. The CP (HL) at $809A is the earth test SetEarthFalls $FB81 patches to NOP.
> Witness: L1 42379 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8084 ScanRowLoop
$8087 ScanCellLoop
$8098 ScanSkipTests
$809A ScanEarthTest
$80D3 ScanNextCell
$80DB c MoveObject ; Make the object at HL fall into DE, or roll it off
> HL = the object, DE = the cell below, B = the column count left (30 for column 29, 1 for column 0). The cell below empty: the object moves into it, HL gets $20; a boulder calls BoulderLandCheck $E78C, another object sets ObjectFell $7FFE. Then the cell under the new place: the player facing right (3) jumps to Crush $9ABC, the rest to MoveObjectLanded $8104. The cell below not empty: RollObject $8117.
> Witness: L1 4511703 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$80EE MarkObjectFell
$80F3 CheckUnderFallen
$8101 b MoveObjectPad ; Leftover: 3 bytes between two jumps, never run
$8104 c MoveObjectLanded ; The cell under the fallen object: the player facing left, or a switch box
> A = the cell. 4 jumps to Crush $9ABC; else LandOnSwitch $810E.
> Witness: L1 15918 (c1, hiscore, rzx x32).
$810B b MoveObjectPad2 ; Leftover: 3 bytes, never run
$810E c LandOnSwitch ; A switch box under a fallen object sets SwitchHit
> A = $0B: SwitchHit $7FFC = $FF. The code that follows ($8117, RollObject) is reached from MoveObject when the cell below is not empty: an object on the player (3, 4), earth (6) or a vacated cell ($20) stays; else it rolls left when it is not in column 0 and the left cell and the one below it are both 0, else right when it is not in column 29 and those are 0.
> Witness: L1 15901 (c1, hiscore, rzx x32).
$8117 RollObject
$8133 RollLeft
$813E TryRollRight
$814B RollRight
$8156 c AntiGravSound ; The anti-gravity sound: falling BEEPER sweeps
> C = $A0 down by 8 a sweep: periods from C + $3C down to C, 2 cycles each. Called by AntiGravStart $A9EF.
> Witness: L1 16 (rzx x6).
$8158 AntiGravSoundLoop
$8161 AntiGravSoundLoop2
$817A c SwitchClear ; After a switch was hit: every force field and switch box becomes $20
> If SwitchHit $7FFC: every cell 9 (force field) and $0B (switch box) becomes $20, SwitchScore $A9E3 (250 points and the sound), SwitchHit = 0. Then AntiGravPass $A7CD: the gravity scan of the pass.
> Witness: L1 43776 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8185 SwitchClearLoop
$8188 SwitchClearLoop2
$818F SwitchClearSkip
$8196 SwitchClearSkip2
$81A3 SwitchClearSkip3
$81A7 b SwitchClearPad ; Leftover: 5 bytes, never run
$81AC c ClearVacated ; Clear the vacated mark of every cell
> Every grid cell AND $1F: $20 becomes 0, the animation codes $10-$1F stay.
> Witness: L1 43775 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$81AF ClearVacatedLoop

@module renderer
$81B9 c AttrAddr ; The attribute address of character cell B, C into HL
> B = the row, C = the column. HL = $5800 + 32B + C.
> Witness: L1 3860 (c1, hiscore, lives, menu, timer, rzx x32).

@module mapscreen
$81CC c ColourMapCells ; Colour the map: each cell's attribute from MapAttrs + its code
> From the last cell back, 20 rows of 30; MapCellAttr $EAB3 writes the attribute (cells from $90 get 0).
> Witness: L1 1 (timer).
$81D1 ColourMapCellsLoop
$81D3 ColourMapCellsLoop2

@module main ; The game flow: the game's start, the cave start, the play loop, the timer, the cave's ends
@about NewGame $8BE5 runs StartGameEntry $89F4: StartGame $85D6 (the password, 5 lives, the score 0), then CaveStart $89F7 for each cave: ClearScreen, the flags 0, CaveIntro $92D4 (the level, the lives, the score, the cave name), the cave's tune (PlayCaveTune $EE34), PlayCave $8885. NextCave $8A07 then takes the next cave (after cave 32 the win screen, then cave 1 again) or a life.
@about A pass of PlayCave: KeysStep $8759 (the player), PutPlayer $8382, AbortKey $93A5 (G), ClearVacated $81AC, WindowOrigin $8DA6 (ViewOrigin, the window placed), MapKey $EA96 (F; its CALL DrawWindowAtOrigin $8D75 draws the window every pass), ColourCycle $81E7 (the gem and exit colours), FizzSound $A773 (the pass sound and the fizz), TimerStep $86DE, QuitKey $872D (H). It ends when CaveOver $FD7D is set (out of time or quit), PlayerKilled $7FFD (DeathView $903F, DeathSound $862E) or CaveDone $FD84 (the exit entered: TimeBonus $8702). The game has no frame sync (no HALT): a pass takes as long as its work and its sounds.

$81E7 c ColourCycle ; Step the cycling colour and flash the open exit
> ColourPhase $FD8E steps; ColourCycleInk $FD8F cycles $43-$46 (DrawPass $8D46 writes it into the gem graphic). Ends with CALL ExitFlash $905B, RET (on either branch).
> Witness: L1 43775 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$81F3 ColourCycleSkip
$81FC ColourCycleSkip2
$820B ColourCycleSkip3
$8210 b ColourCyclePad ; Leftover: CALL $8059, CALL $81CC, CALL $81E7, RET (10 bytes), never run
$821A c ClearVars ; Clear the variables and the cave grid, $FD7A-$FFFF
> HL = $FD7A, DE = HL + 1, BC = $028A, (HL) = 0, LDIR: the copy runs on past $FFFF into $0000-$0004 (the ROM: no effect).
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, lives, menu).

