@module unpack ; The cave unpacker and the cave's set-up
@about Each cave is 314 bytes at CaveData + 314 x (N - 1) (N = 1-32; the code computes $BEC6 + 314N): 300 bytes of two cells each (the low nibble first) for the 30 x 20 grid, then 14 parameter bytes copied to CaveParams $FD9A. CaveSetup $9313 unpacks the cave, writes the earth and wall graphics into the cell table and colours the exit door, the boulder and two more graphics.

$82B6 c UnpackCave ; Unpack cave CaveNumber into the grid and copy its 14 parameters
> HL = $BEC6 + 314 x CaveNumber $FD91; 300 bytes give 600 cells (low nibble first) into CaveGrid $FDA8, then 14 bytes to CaveParams $FD9A.
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$82C0 UnpackCaveLoop
$82C9 UnpackCaveLoop2

@module main
$82E6 c ResetGame ; The first cave, 4 lives, the colour phase
> ColourPhase $FD8E = 1, CaveNumber $FD91 = 1, Lives $FD93 = 4, Unused99 $FD90 = 99. StartGame $85D6 sets 5 lives later.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, lives, menu).

@module effects
$82F9 c GemSound ; The gem sound
> ROM BEEPER HL = $0200, DE = 5, then HL = $0100, DE = 10.
> Witness: L1 1692 (c1, rzx x32).

@module hud ; The HUD, the score, the time bar, the digits and the texts
@about The bottom line (row 23) shows the cave, the gems needed and taken (needed : taken), the lives (ShowCounters $85AD) and the score (ShowScore $8342); the time bar is 4 pixel lines at $52C0 (row 22). Numbers are strings of decimal digits (0-9 a byte) printed with the digit glyphs at $BD80 (PrintDigits $832A); texts are ASCII printed with the font, glyph $BC00 + 8 x code (PrintText $834F).

$8315 c IncDigits ; Add 1 to a decimal digit string
> HL = the last digit, B = the digits. The carry runs left while a digit wraps from 9 to 0.
> Witness: L1 70724 (c1, rzx x32).
$8321 c AddPoint ; Add 1 point to the score
> IncDigits on ScoreDigits $FD94-$FD99.
> Witness: L1 61961 (c1, rzx x32).
$832A c PrintDigits ; Print D decimal digits right to left
> HL = the last digit, B = the row, C = the last digit's column, D = the count. The glyph of digit k is $BD80 + 8k.
> Witness: L1 82595 (c1, hiscore, lives, menu, timer, rzx x32).
$8342 c ShowScore ; Print the score at row 23, columns 26-31
> Witness: L1 12605 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$834F c PrintText ; Print D characters of ASCII text
> HL = the text, B = the row, C = the first column, D = the length. The glyph of code k is $BC00 + 8k (Font $BD00 is code $20).
> Witness: L1 5918 (c1, hiscore, lives, menu, timer, rzx x32).
$8359 PrintTextLoop
$836A c ShowHudLine ; Print HudLine $BCE0 on row 23
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8376 c AddGemValue ; Add GemValue $FD9B points, one at a time
> Witness: L1 1692 (c1, rzx x32).
$837A AddGemValueLoop
$8382 c PutPlayer ; Write the player's code at the player's cell
> CaveGrid + PlayerIndex = PlayerFacing $FD86.
> Witness: L1 43776 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$838E c FaceLeft ; PlayerFacing = 4 (facing left)
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8394 c CountGem ; Count a gem; open the exit when enough are taken
> GemCount $FD92 + 1; when it equals GemsNeeded $FD9A, ExitOpen $FD85 = $FF. Then GemDigits $FD82 + 1 (IncDigits $8315: the gems taken, counting up from 00), printed at row 23 (PrintDigits, BC = $1709), and GemSound $82F9.
> Witness: rzx-earth01 frame 814, the panel goes from 00 to 01.
> Witness: L1 1692 (c1, rzx x32).
$83A6 CountGemSkip

@module player ; The player: the keys, the moves, digging, pushing, the special cells
@about PlayerStep $8556 tries the direction keys in the order left, right, up, down; the first that moves the player sets KeyMoved $FD80 and ends the step, so a pass moves the player at most one cell. PlayerIndex $FD9C is the player's cell (0-599); PlayerFacing $FD86 is the player's code: 3 right, 4 left. The key sites are self-modified (see the keys module).
@about A move into earth (6) or empty (0) moves the player; earth sets DugEarth $E857 (the dig noise). A wall (5), a closed exit (1) and the cave's edge block. A boulder (2) moves left or right when the cell beyond is empty (PushBoulder $E81F); never up or down. A gem (7) is taken (CollectGem $8595). The codes 8-$0F have their handlers through LeftSpecial $94D6, RightSpecial $9494, UpSpecial $9414, DownSpecial $93CE. With the fire key held (FireStep $8878) the direction key acts on the next cell without moving the player.

$83C3 c TryLeft ; The left key: move or act to the left
> The key site LD A,row ($83C4) / AND mask ($83CA) is written by RedefineKeys $8C30 and the control choice. Pressed: PlayerFacing = 4, KeyMoved = $FF; column 0 stops; the exit (1) only when ExitOpen (then CaveDone); the wall test BlockWall $E869, boulders PushBoulder $E81F, the codes > 6 LeftSpecial $94D6 (which takes gems and the other specials, continuation MoveLeft); then MoveLeft $8428.
> Witness: L1 42086 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$83DE TryLeftLoop
$83FB TryLeftSkip
$8409 TryLeftLoop2
$841E TryLeftSkip2
$8428 c MoveLeft ; Move the player one cell left (the old cell 0)
> Witness: L1 4366 (c1, rzx x32).
$8437 c TryRight ; The right key: move or act to the right
> As TryLeft $83C3 with PlayerFacing = 3, column 29 the edge, RightSpecial $9494 (continuation MoveRight), MoveRight $849E.
> Witness: L1 36883 (c1, hiscore, lives, timer, rzx x32).
$8453 TryRightLoop
$8470 TryRightSkip
$847F TryRightLoop2
$8494 TryRightSkip2
