@module menu ; The menu, the title, the screen wipes
@about GameEntry $8B20 (the BASIC's RANDOMIZE USR 35616) clears the variables, draws the title (DrawTitle $8AC8: the texts, the logo wiped in line by line, its colours), plays the title tune and reads keys 1-5 (MenuKeys $8B29): 1 a game, 2 redefine the keys, 3 keyboard, 4 joystick, 5 reset. When the title tune runs out the high scores and the scroller show (ShowHiScores $B2E4), then the title tune again if the scroller ran out; a key 1-5 that stops the scroller is acted on at once.

$85CF c ResetAll ; Clear the variables and set the start values
> ClearVars $821A, ResetGame $82E6.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, lives, menu).

@module password ; The password entry and the cave name table
@about The passwords are the cave names: CaveNames $9700 holds 32 names of 20 characters, space padded. EnterPassword $8E2D reads up to 20 characters into PasswordBuffer $FD00; FindPassword $8E91 compares it with 50 records of 20 bytes from $9700 (records 33-50 run past the names over zeros, code and data; they never match a typed name). A match starts the game at that cave; no match (ENTER alone too) at cave 1.

$85D6 c StartGame ; Start a game: the password, 5 lives, the score 0
> CaveDigits $FD7E = 0, 1; Password $8F29 (sets the cave); Lives $FD93 = 5, ScoreDigits 0.
> Witness: L1 3 (c1, lives, rzx x1).

