@module keys ; The keys: the key table, the redefinition, keyboard or joystick
@about The keys are read by self-modified code: TryLeft $83C3, TryRight $8437, TryUp $84AD, TryDown $84F9 and KeysStep $8759 each start LD A,row; OUT ($FF),A; IN A,($FE); AND mask (the OUT to port $FF has no effect: no 48K device decodes an odd port; IN A,($FE) puts A on the high address byte itself). RedefineKeys $8C30 takes a key with WaitKey $8C1D (KeyTable $A900: 40 records of half row, bit mask, character) and writes its row and mask into the sites. Keys 3 and 4 of the menu copy whole 9-byte code fragments into the sites: KeyboardControl $EBCA the copies saved at KeyboardCode $EB15, JoystickControl $EC2E the Kempston fragments KempstonCode $EAC4 (IN A,($1F) and a bit test).

$8C0E c Pause ; Wait 30 x 256 loop turns, then LineAddr
> Witness: L1 576 (c1, lives, menu).
$8C11 PauseLoop
$8C13 PauseSkip
$8C1D c WaitKey ; Wait until a key of KeyTable is down
> Scans the 40 records over and over. Out: HL = the record's mask byte, the character at HL + 1.
> No release wait: a key still down when WaitKey is called again is taken again (the menu recording's redefinition took 2 for left, right and up).
> Witness: L1 69199 (c1, hiscore, lives, menu, rzx x1).
$8C22 WaitKeyLoop
$8C30 c RedefineKeys ; Key 2: define the left, right, up, down and fire keys
> ClearAndKeyboard $ECDC; for each prompt of KeyPrompts $A978: WaitKey, the key's character printed, its row and mask written into the key sites ($83C4 / $83CA, $876C / $8772 ...), RaspSound $90A0.
> Starts with ClearAndKeyboard: the keyboard code is back in the sites before the keys are written, so a redefinition always selects the keyboard. The fire prompt writes KeysStep only.
> Witness: L1 2 (c1, menu).
$8C35 RedefineKeysLoop

